          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "બચત (bacat) is built on the verb bacvũ, \"to be left over\", with the noun ending -at: what is left over. bacvũ came into Gujarati from Hindi and goes back to Sanskrit váñcati, \"escapes from\" (CDIAL 11208)."
            }
          ]
        },
